hadiths[6]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1204","'Abu Bakr as-Siddiq asked the Prophet,\nmay Allah bless him and grant him peace, \Messenger of Allah"," teach me\nwhat to say in the mornings and evenings.\"" He said"," \""Abu Bakr"," say"," 'O\nAllah"," the Creator of the heavens and the earth"," the Knower of the Unseen\nand Visible. the Lord of all things and their Master. I seek refuge with\nYou from the evil of shaytan and his encouragement to associate and that\nI bring evil on myself or bring it on another Muslim.'\""'\"""""
"1205","It is narrated from Abū Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, that when the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, would rise in the morning, he would supplicate: \O Allah"," by Your favour we have reached the morning"," and by Your favour we reach the evening. By Your favour we live and in Your name we die"," and to You is the resurrection.\"" And when he would enter the evening"," he would say: \""O Allah"," by Your favour we have reached the evening"," and by Your favour we reach the morning. By Your favour we live and in Your name we die"," and to You is the return.\""\nAl-Adab al-Mufrad"," Hadith: 1205; Arabic Hadith: 1205"""
"1206","It is narrated from Ibn ʿUmar, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, would never omit these words in the morning and evening: \O Allah"," I ask You for well-being in this world and the Hereafter. O Allah"," I ask You for pardon"," well-being"," and protection in my religion"," my worldly affairs"," my family"," and my wealth. O Allah"," conceal my faults and grant me security from the things I fear. O Allah"," protect me from before me"," from behind me"," from my right"," from my left"," and from above me. And I seek refuge in Your Magnificence lest I be destroyed suddenly from beneath me.\""\nAl-Adab al-Mufrad"," Hadith: 1206; Arabic Hadith: 1206"""
"1207","Sayyiduna Anas ibn Mālik (may Allāh be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allāh (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \Whoever says in the morning: 'O Allāh"," we have reached the morning"," and we call You as witness"," and we call the bearers of Your Throne"," Your other angels"," and all of Your creation as witnesses that You are Allāh"," there is no deity worthy of worship except You"," You alone"," without any partner"," and indeed Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) is Your servant and Your Messenger' — Allāh"," the Most High"," shall free one-fourth of him from the Hellfire on that day. And if he says it twice"," Allāh shall free half of him from the Hellfire. And if he says it four times"," Allāh shall free him entirely from the Hellfire on that day.\""\n\n*Al-Adab al-Mufrad"," Hadith: 1207; Arabic Hadith: 1207*"""
"1208","Sayyiduna Abū Hurayrah (may Allāh be pleased with him) narrates that Sayyiduna Abū Bakr (may Allāh be pleased with him) submitted: \O Messenger of Allāh! Teach me a supplication that I may recite in the morning and evening.\"" He (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \""Recite: 'O Allāh"," Knower of the unseen and the seen"," Creator of the heavens and the earth"," Lord and Sovereign of all things. I bear witness that there is no deity worthy of worship except You. I seek refuge in You from the evil of my own self"," from the evil of Shayṭān"," and from his shirk (associating partners with You).' Recite this in the morning"," in the evening"," and when you go to sleep.\""\n\n*Al-Adab al-Mufrad"," Hadith: 1208; Arabic Hadith: 1208*"""
"1209","Sayyiduna Abū Hurayrah (may Allāh be pleased with him) narrates in a similar manner to the first hadith. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \Lord and Sovereign of all things.\"" And he also said: \""From the evil of Shayṭān and from his shirk.\""\n\n*Al-Adab al-Mufrad"," Hadith: 1209; Arabic Hadith: 1209*"""
